Spec: specs/001-core-and-anthropic-passthrough/spec.md (AC30, AC31, AC47, AC48)
ADR: docs/decisions/0003-reverseproxy-with-rewrite-as-proxy-engine.md
Research: Q8, Q12, Q13 (499), Q19 (short body is a disconnect)
Why this approach: classify(ctx, m, err) takes the inbound context and returns 499 with an empty reason as its first branch; handleError then sets Meta.ClientDisconnected and writes the header only (no body, no x-gateway-error, no gateway_error). After headers nothing changes: ReverseProxy panics http.ErrAbortHandler and T7's Settle in the access-log defer decides upstream_aborted versus client_disconnected.
Q19 precondition: TestNetHTTP_ChunkedFramingErrorKeepsContextLive (plain net/http, no proxy) shows the handler's body read fails on "zz" chunk framing while r.Context().Err() stays nil (20 runs under -race), so the 400 branch stays reachable behind the context branch. plan.md error-handler step 2 now names this test.
Tests moved from T10: TestProxy_MalformedClientBody400 is now three subtests: broken chunked framing on a live connection (no half-close) is 400 client_body; short of Content-Length plus half-close is 499, empty body, no x-gateway-error, client_disconnected; a client that closes mid-chunked-body is logged 499, bytes 0, client_disconnected. TestProxy_ClientBodyBeatsTimeout now uses a real broken chunked body (httputil.NewChunkedReader) and adds a cancelled-context row (499 beats the body error).
Alternatives rejected: a separate branch in handleError ahead of classify (the order would live in two places and TestProxy_ClientBodyBeatsTimeout could not pin it through Classify).
Helpers: bodyTolerantUpstream, gateway.dial, checkClientDisconnected, holdingUpstream (holds until its request context is cancelled, optionally after one SSE event), await, leaveMidStream, dyingUpstream (raw listener: headers plus one chunk, then close without terminator).
Verified by: new tests first failed for the right reasons (400/502 where 499 expected, gateway_error present, classify 400 where 499 expected). Passing on arrival (resting on T7's Settle): ClientDisconnectCancelsUpstream/mid-stream, UpstreamDiesMidStreamAbortsClient, AccessLog_UpstreamAbortedField; proved by making Settle a no-op (mid-stream and both abort rows fail) and by having the response watcher turn an upstream read error into io.EOF (AC31 sees a clean end, upstream_aborted missing); both reverted. Every proxy test that ends in a cancel or abort runs checkNoLeaksAtEnd. go test -race -count=15 on the error/abort tests; make verify.
